          "number": 10,
          "letter": "J",
          "english": "This refers to the idea that when objects trying to resemble humans aren't quite perfect, they can make viewers feel uneasy because they fall somewhere between obviously non-human and fully human. \"That's always a danger when you're doing anything human or human-like,\" says Webber. \"There're a thousand things that could go wrong with a computer-generated facial performance, and any one of those could make it fall into the uncanny valley,\" he says: \"Your brain just knows there's something wrong.\" The problem often arises around the eyes or mouth, says Webber. \"They're the areas that you look at when you're talking to someone.\"",
          "chinese": "这指的是这样一种观点：当试图模仿人类的物体不够完美时，它们会让观众感到不安，因为它们处于明显非人类与完全人类之间的某个状态。韦伯说：“当你制作任何具有人类特征或类似人类的东西时，这始终是一种危险。计算机生成的面部表演可能有成千上万种出错的方式，其中任何一种都可能使它落入诡异谷。”他还说：“你的大脑就是知道有哪里不对劲。”韦伯说，问题通常出现在眼睛或嘴巴周围。“这些正是你与某人交谈时会注视的部位。”",
