          "english": "You can't see it, smell it, or hear it, and people disagree on how precisely to define it, or where exactly it comes from. It isn't a school subject or an academic discipline, but it can be learned. It is a quality that is required of artists, but it is also present in the lives of scientists and entrepreneurs. All of us benefit from it and we thrive mentally and spiritually when we are able to wield it. It is a delicate thing, easily stamped out; in fact, it flourishes most fully when people are playful and childlike. Meanwhile, it works best in conjunction with deep knowledge and expertise.",
          "chinese": "你看不见它，闻不到它，也听不见它；人们对于如何准确界定它，或者它究竟来自何处，意见并不一致。它不是一门学校课程，也不是一门学术学科，但可以通过学习获得。艺术家需要具备这种品质，但科学家和企业家的生活中也同样存在这种品质。我们所有人都能从中受益；当我们能够运用它时，精神和心灵都会得到蓬勃发展。这是一种脆弱的东西，很容易被扼杀；事实上，只有在人们保持顽皮、天真如孩童时，它才能最充分地成长。同时，它与深厚的知识和专业技能结合时，效果最佳。",
